      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"quantitative_comparisons\": [\n    {\n      \"group_definitions\": {\n        \"d-FMT\": \"Donor Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (active intervention)\",\n        \"p-FMT\": \"Placebo Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (control)\"\n      },\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"d-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"24.0 months\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"group\": \"p-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"9.0 months\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"research_object\": \"Median Progression-Free Survival (mPFS) in TACITO trial\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase 2a randomized trial in metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"group_definitions\": {\n        \"d-FMT\": \"Donor Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (active intervention)\",\n        \"p-FMT\": \"Placebo Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (control)\"\n      },\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"d-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"70%\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"group\": \"p-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"41%\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"research_object\": \"12-month Progression-Free Survival rate in TACITO trial\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase 2a randomized trial in metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"group_definitions\": {\n        \"d-FMT\": \"Donor Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (active intervention)\",\n        \"p-FMT\": \"Placebo Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (control)\"\n      },\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"d-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"52%\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"group\": \"p-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"32%\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"research_object\": \"Objective Response Rate (ORR) in TACITO trial\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase 2a randomized trial in metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"group_definitions\": {},\n      \"groups\": [],\n      \"research_object\": \"Clinical outcomes in MITRIC trial\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Single-arm phase IIa basket trial in ICI-refractory solid cancers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"group_definitions\": {},\n      \"groups\": [],\n      \"research_object\": \"Clinical outcomes in MIMic trial\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Single-arm Phase I trial in advanced melanoma, anti-PD1 monotherapy\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usable_content\": \"现有证据尚未证实已完成的大规模随机对照 III 期试验确认微生物组干预在 ICI 治疗患者中的疗效。目前发表的最高级别证据为 2025 年发布的 TACITO 试验，这是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）患者的研究者发起的、随机、双盲、安慰剂对照的 **IIa 期** 试验。该试验评估了来自 ICI 完全缓解者的粪菌移植（FMT）联合帕博利珠单抗和阿昔替尼一线治疗的疗效。结果显示，虽然主要终点（12个月无进展生存率，d-FMT 70% vs p-FMT 41%, P=0.053）未达到统计学显著性，但次要终点中位无进展生存期（mPFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月; HR=0.50, P=0.035），客观缓解率（ORR）也更高（52% vs 32%）。然而，总生存期（OS）的差异未达统计学显著性（41.0个月 vs 28.3个月, P=0.167）。相比之下，其他相关研究如 MITRIC 试验（单臂 IIa 期，ICI 难治性实体瘤）显示 FMT 作为挽救治疗无效（ORR 0%），而 MIMic 试验（单臂 I 期，黑色素瘤）虽报告了较好的生存数据，但因缺乏对照组且样本量小，仅为假设生成性研究。因此，尽管有 IIa 期 RCT 提示潜在获益，但目前仍缺乏完成的、大规模的 III 期 RCT 来确证其疗效。\",\n  \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n  \"still_missing\": \"需要检索并确认是否存在已完成的、大规模（通常指多中心、大样本）的 III 期随机对照试验（RCT），特别是那些以总生存期（OS）或明确的无进展生存期（PFS）为主要终点的试验，以证实微生物组干预（如 FMT 或特定菌群制剂）在 ICI 治疗患者中的确切疗效。目前的材料仅提供了 IIa 期 RCT 和早期单臂试验的数据。\",\n  \"read_focus\": \"\",\n  \"external_ask\": \"请检索并列出所有已完成的、公开发表的关于粪菌移植（FMT）或定义明确的微生物组制剂与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）联合使用的大型 III 期随机对照试验（RCT）。重点关注试验阶段（Phase III）、随机对照设计、主要结局指标（OS/PFS/ORR）及其统计显著性。特别关注黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌等常见实体瘤领域的此类试验。\",\n  \"reason\": \"当前提供的材料中，最高级别的证据是 TACITO 试验，但其明确标注为 Phase 2a 试验，且主要终点未达标，次要终点虽显著但需更大规模验证。MITRIC 和 MIMic 均为单臂早期试验，不具备 RCT 的证据等级。问题明确要求“已完成的、大规模随机对照 III 期试验”，现有材料未能满足这一核心标准，因此判定为 external_research，需要进一步检索是否有符合该严格定义的 III 期 RCT 结果。\"\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "Here's a thinking process:\n\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\n    *   **Role:** Review author's material reading assistant.\n    *   **Task:** Extract specific research insights around a writing question from `material_found` and `paper_context`. Keep research objects/materials, settings, comparisons, methods, operations/conditions, results/arguments, validation methods, and applicable boundaries. Use cards/expert summaries/original text based on content relevance, not format.\n    *   **Constraints:**\n        *   Understand `user_scope` and question object. Do not substitute with other objects/methods/settings/comparisons.\n        *   No unwarranted extrapolation. Correlation != causation. Methods don't automatically prove causality/confounding control/independent validation unless explicitly stated.\n        *   Output `usable_content` as a readable string: specific insights, similarities/differences, explanations, conditions. Start with findings that distinguish studies, end with distinctions. Don't synthesize different objects/settings into one universal mechanism.\n        *   Handle numbers carefully: First output `quantitative_comparisons`, then `usable_content`. Each item in `quantitative_comparisons`: `research_object`, `result_or_measure`, `setting_or_time`, `groups` (list of `{group: name, value: number+unit}`). Preserve original order/names. Define abbreviations separately. Read numbers exactly next to group names. Record `reported_statistics`. One number per group. Overall vs stratified are separate. `usable_content` explains meaning, doesn't repeat/rearrange numbers. No fabrication.\n        *   If question limits to specific setting/time/subgroup, read overall and specified parts separately.\n        *   `decision`: Judge if the *specific question* is resolved. `direct_use`=enough to answer or corrects false premise; `local_deep_read`=need another part/full comparison; `external_research`=missing new object/method/comparison/validation. `external_research` can still have rich `usable_content` but must state remaining gap. Don't declare `direct_use` just because materials exist. Correct assumptions in the question.\n        *   For \"does X type of study/result exist?\" questions, one matching instance answers it. Absence in several papers or an old review saying \"none at the time\" doesn't answer current existence. Existing content shows landscape up to that source's time. If later confirmation is needed, choose `external_research` with specific retrieval request. Only give negative answer if question explicitly limits to these sources' time/materials.\n        *   `reading_mode=focused_local_read` already executed supplementary reading.\n        *   Order: `quantitative_comparisons` first, then `usable_content`. Must read original sentences for each group, don't guess direction. If reverse/no difference, state inconsistency upfront. Overall vs stratified are not interchangeable.\n        *   Return JSON with fields in order: `quantitative_comparisons`, `usable_content`, `decision`, `still_missing`, `read_focus`, `external_ask`, `reason`.\n\n2.  **Deconstruct the Question & Scope:**\n    *   **Question:** \"是否存在已完成的、大规模随机对照 III 期试验证实微生物组干预在 ICI 治疗患者中的疗效？\" (Are there completed, large-scale randomized controlled Phase III trials confirming the efficacy of microbiome interventions in patients treated with ICIs?)\n    *   **User Scope:** \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\" (Contextual, but the direct question is about Phase III RCTs).\n    *   **Success Criteria:** Confirm if Phase III RCTs are completed and published with primary outcome data (OS/PFS), or confirm 'unmet' status.\n    *   **Materials Provided:**\n        *   MITRIC trial (Phase IIa, single-arm basket trial, n=12, advanced cancers progressing on ICIs). Results: ORR 0%, mPFS 1.5 mo, mOS 10.1 mo. Safe/feasible. Mechanistic insights on engraftment/transience, immune signatures.\n        *   TACITO trial (Phase 2a, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, n=45, treatment-naive mRCC receiving pembro + axitinib). Primary endpoint (12-mo PFS rate) not met (70% vs 41%, P=0.053). Secondary (median PFS) met (24.0 vs 9.0 mo, HR=0.50, P=0.035). OS trend not significant. Mechanistic: strain engraftment linked to outcomes.\n        *   MIMic trial (Phase I, single-arm, n=20, advanced melanoma, anti-PD1 + healthy donor FMT). ORR 65%, mPFS 29.6 mo, mOS 52.8 mo. Compared to historical RCTs. Explicitly hypothesis-generating, small sample, no control. Mentions planned Phase II ME.17.\n    *   **Key Finding regarding Question:** All provided trials are Phase I or Phase IIa. None are Phase III. The materials explicitly state this limitation and note that Phase III confirmation is pending/unmet. Therefore, the answer to the specific question is \"No, currently unmet based on available evidence.\"\n\n3.  **Extract Quantitative Comparisons:**\n    *   Need to list groups, results, settings, etc., strictly from the text.\n    *   *MITRIC:* Group: d-FMT (ICI responders donors), Setting: Phase IIa single-arm basket trial, ICI-refractory solid tumors (melanoma, HNSCC, RCC, MSI-H pancreatic cancer). Result: ORR 0%, mPFS 1.5 months, mOS 10.1 months. Stats: None reported for these primary endpoints besides descriptive.\n    *   *TACITO:* Groups: d-FMT (donor FMT), p-FMT (placebo FMT). Setting: Phase 2a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, treatment-naive mRCC receiving pembrolizumab + axitinib. Results: 12-month PFS rate: d-FMT 70%, p-FMT 41% (P=0.053); Median PFS: d-FMT 24.0 months, p-FMT 9.0 months (HR=0.50, P=0.035); Median OS: d-FMT 41.0 months, p-FMT 28.3 months (P=0.167). ORR: d-FMT 52%, p-FMT 32%.\n    *   *MIMic:* Group: FMT + anti-PD1. Setting: Phase I multicenter single-arm trial, advanced melanoma. Result: ORR 65%, mPFS 29.6 months, mOS 52.8 months. Stats: None reported (historical comparison only).\n    *   Let's structure `quantitative_comparisons` carefully according to instructions.\n    *   Item 1: MITRIC trial. research_object: FMT from ICI responders. result_or_measure: Objective response rate (ORR), median progression-free survival (mPFS), median overall survival (mOS). setting_or_time: Phase IIa single-arm basket trial, ICI-refractory solid tumors. groups: [{group: \"FMT group\", value: \"ORR 0%; mPFS 1.5 months; mOS 10.1 months\"}]. reported_statistics: []\n    *   Item 2: TACITO trial. research_object: FMT from complete ICI responders combined with pembrolizumab + axitinib. result_or_measure: 12-month PFS rate, median PFS, median OS, ORR. setting_or_time: Phase 2a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, treatment-naive metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC). groups: [{group: \"d-FMT\", value: \"12-month PFS 70%; median PFS 24.0 months; median OS 41.0 months; ORR 52%\"}, {group: \"p-FMT\", value: \"12-month PFS 41%; median PFS 9.0 months; median OS 28.3 months; ORR 32%\"}]. reported_statistics: [\n  \"12-month PFS P=0.053\",\n  \"median PFS HR=0.50, P=0.035\",\n  \"median OS P=0.167\"\n]\n    *   Item 3: MIMic trial. research_object: Oral FMT from healthy donors combined with anti-PD1 therapy. result_or_measure: Objective response rate (ORR), median progression-free survival (mPFS), median overall survival (mOS). setting_or_time: Phase I multicenter single-arm trial, advanced melanoma. groups: [{group: \"FMT + anti-PD1\", value: \"ORR 65%; mPFS 29.6 months; mOS 52.8 months\"}]. reported_statistics: []\n    *   Check constraints: \"一组一数成对，不用多组名字对应一串数字\". I will split them to be safe, or keep them paired as requested. The prompt says \"groups 是 [{group:原文组名或缩写,value:紧邻该组的结果含单位}]\". I'll follow that.\n    *   Let's refine `quantitative_comparisons` to strictly match the format.\n    *   I will list each trial's quantitative data clearly.\n\n4.  **Draft `usable_content`:**\n    *   Focus on answering the question while providing mechanistic/contextual insights as per scope.\n    *   Start with distinguishing findings: Current evidence comes exclusively from early-phase trials (Phase I/IIa) rather than completed Phase III RCTs.\n    *   MITRIC (Phase IIa, refractory): Shows limited clinical activity (ORR 0%), transient engraftment, and highlights that baseline myeloid-dominant environment/high IL-8 correlates with poor outcomes, while activated T-cell signature is favorable. These immune features reflect host disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Efficacy appears highly context-dependent, possibly due to rapid disease progression not allowing time for microbiota modulation.\n    *   TACITO (Phase 2a, treatment-naive mRCC): Randomized design shows median PFS benefit (24.0 vs 9.0 months) but misses primary 12-month PFS rate endpoint. Strain-level engraftment (e.g., *Blautia wexlerae*) associates with better PFS, while *Akkermansia massiliensis* acquisition links to worse PFS. Suggests specific strain interactions matter more than total engraftment, and timing (first-line vs refractory) critically influences efficacy.\n    *   MIMic (Phase I, melanoma): Reports high ORR (65%) and prolonged survival compared to historical controls, with SCFA-producing taxa enrichment in responders. However, lacks control arm and explicit randomization, limiting causal inference.\n    *   Synthesis for the question: No completed Phase III RCTs confirming efficacy exist in the current literature base. The available Phase IIa/II data demonstrate safety and feasibility but yield inconsistent efficacy signals heavily dependent on disease stage (refractory vs. treatment-naïve), donor selection, and microbial strain dynamics. Reliable biomarkers for patient selection remain unestablished.\n    *   Ensure tone matches constraints: No overgeneralization, clear distinction between studies, addresses the Phase III question directly, preserves mechanistic nuances (engraftment transience, strain-specific effects, immune milieu reflection vs modification).\n\n5.  **Determine `decision`, `still_missing`, `read_focus`, `external_ask`, `reason`:**\n    *   `decision`: `external_research` (The question specifically asks for completed Phase III RCTs. The provided materials explicitly state they are Phase I/IIa and do not meet the criterion. While they provide strong supporting context, the core requirement for Phase III confirmation is unmet.)\n    *   `still_missing`: Completed Phase III randomized controlled trial data confirming OS/PFS benefit of microbiome interventions (FMT or defined consortia) combined with ICIs in solid tumors.\n    *   `read_focus`: N/A (already initial read, but if needed, focus on registry updates or recent publications post-2025/2026 for Phase III completion status).\n    *   `external_ask`: Retrieve completed Phase III RCTs evaluating FMT or defined microbial consortia with ICIs in oncology (e.g., verify completion and primary endpoint results of TACITO's potential expansion, or identify other registered Phase III trials like those in melanoma/RCC mentioned in planning notes).\n    *   `reason`: 提供的材料均为I期或IIa期研究（MITRIC单臂IIa期、TACITO双盲安慰剂对照IIa期、MIMic单臂I期），明确说明尚未完成III期试验。现有数据虽显示安全性与可行性，但疗效高度依赖疾病阶段、供体选择及菌株定植特征，且缺乏大样本随机对照验证。需检索已完成的III期RCT以确认疗效是否得到最终证实。\n\n6.  **Self-Correction/Verification during drafting:**\n    *   Check `quantitative_comparisons` format: Must be a list of objects with `research_object`, `result_or_measure`, `setting_or_time`, `groups`, `reported_statistics`.\n    *   I will structure it carefully.\n    *   Check `usable_content`: Starts with distinguishing findings, ends with distinctions. Explains meaning without repeating numbers. Addresses the question. Matches scope.\n    *   Check decision logic: Question asks \"是否存在已完成的...III期试验...\". Materials say none. So `external_research` is correct. I will state that the current evidence stops at Phase IIa, and Phase III confirmation remains pending.\n    *   Check constraints: \"先呈现能区别不同研究的发现或论证，不先套领域常见结论；结尾也要保留这些区别。\" -> I will ensure the opening contrasts the refractory vs naive settings and single-arm vs RCT designs, and closing reiterates the context-dependency and lack of Phase III data.\n    *   Check numbers: I extracted them exactly. I'll format them properly.\n    *   One detail: TACITO's primary endpoint was 12-month PFS rate. I'll note it accurately.\n    *   All good. Proceed to generate JSON. \n    *   Structure check:\n      ```json\n      {\n        \"quantitative_comparisons\": [...],\n        \"usable_content\": \"...\",\n        \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n        \"still_missing\": \"...\",\n        \"read_focus\": \"...\",\n        \"external_ask\": \"...\",\n        \"reason\": \"...\"\n      }\n      ```\n    *   Refine `quantitative_comparisons` to strictly follow: `[{research_object, result_or_measure, setting_or_time, groups, reported_statistics}, ...]`\n    *   I will make sure each item corresponds to one trial/study for clarity, as requested.\n    *   Check `groups` format: `[{group: \"d-FMT\", value: \"70%\"}, {group: \"p-FMT\", value: \"41%\"}]` etc. I'll split complex results into separate items if needed, or keep them grouped per trial as long as values are adjacent to group names. The prompt says \"一组一数成对，不用多组名字对应一串数字\". I will split them to be strictly compliant.\n    *   Let's construct carefully. \n    *   Item 1: MITRIC. research_object: FMT from ICI responders. result_or_measure: Objective response rate (ORR). setting_or_time: Phase IIa single-arm basket trial, ICI-refractory solid tumors. groups: [{group: \"FMT group\", value: \"0%\"}]. reported_statistics: [].\n    *   Item 2: MITRIC. result_or_measure: median progression-free survival (mPFS). groups: [{group: \"FMT group\", value: \"1.5 months\"}].\n    *   Item 3: MITRIC. result_or_measure: median overall survival (mOS). groups: [{group: \"FMT group\", value: \"10.1 months\"}].\n    *   Item 4: TACITO. result_or_measure: 12-month PFS rate. groups: [{group: \"d-FMT\", value: \"70%\"}, {group: \"p-FMT\", value: \"41%\"}]. reported_statistics: [\"P=0.053\"].\n    *   Item 5: TACITO. result_or_measure: median PFS. groups: [{group: \"d-FMT\", value: \"24.0 months\"}, {group: \"p-FMT\", value: \"9.0 months\"}]. reported_statistics: [\"HR=0.50, P=0.035\"].\n    *   Item 6: TACITO. result_or_measure: median OS. groups: [{group: \"d-FMT\", value: \"41.0 months\"}, {group: \"p-FMT\", value: \"28.3 months\"}]. reported_statistics: [\"P=0.167\"].\n    *   Item 7: TACITO. result_or_measure: ORR. groups: [{group: \"d-FMT\", value: \"52%\"}, {group: \"p-FMT\", value: \"32%\"}].\n    *   Item 8: MIMIC. result_or_measure: ORR. groups: [{group: \"FMT + anti-PD1\", value: \"65%\"}].\n    *   Item 9: MIMIC. result_or_measure: mPFS. groups: [{group: \"FMT + anti-PD1\", value: \"29.6 months\"}].\n    *   Item 10: MIMIC. result_or_measure: mOS. groups: [{group: \"FMT + anti-PD1\", value: \"52.8 months\"}].\n    *   This strictly follows \"一组一数成对\". I will combine them logically but keep the structure clean. Actually, the prompt says \"groups 是 [{group:原文组名或缩写,value:紧邻该组的结果含单位}]\". I'll stick to one entry per metric per trial for simplicity and compliance.\n    *   Wait, the prompt says \"逐字读取每个组名紧随的数值，不从常识、总体结论或组名列表反推配对。一组一数成对，不用多组名字对应一串数字；总体与分层比较、不同指标或结果分别",
